 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "**Result: 24 failed, 1 error, 462 passed, 1 skipped.**\n\n**Main root cause:** `src/tessel/sessions.py:374` passes `partitioned=...` to `response.set_cookie()` (and to `delete_cookie()`), but the installed Werkzeug's `Response.set_cookie()` doesn't accept that keyword. It raises `TypeError: Response.set_cookie() got an unexpected keyword argument 'partitioned'`. The installed Werkzeug is likely older than the version this code expects (`partitioned` was added in Werkzeug 3.1).\n\nThis accounts for 19 of the 24 failures, all of them any test that writes a session cookie:\n- 13 in `test_basic.py` (the session and flash tests)\n- `test_helpers.py::test_stream_keeps_session`\n- `test_reqctx.py::test_copy_context_thread`\n- `test_signals.py::test_flash_signal`\n- `test_templating.py::test_standard_context`\n- 3 in `test_testing.py`\n\nThe `ERROR` in `test_helpers.py::TestStreaming::test_stream_keeps_session` appears to be a teardown assertion following that same failure.\n\n**Remaining 5 failures** (not investigated in depth, and likely unrelated or partly related):\n- `test_helpers.py::TestStreaming::test_async_view` raises a `RuntimeError`, likely a missing async dependency.\n- `test_helpers.py::test_open_resource_exceptions[a]` is a pytest-raises mismatch.\n- `test_reqctx.py::test_session_dynamic_cookie_name` is an `AssertionError`, possibly the same cookie issue.\n- `test_request.py::test_limit_config` fails on `assert None...`, probably a config or version difference.\n\nNothing was changed.",
